# Johan: "At the beginning of combat on your turn, you may have Johan gain "Johan can't attack" until end of combat. If you
# do, attacking doesn't cause creatures you control to tap this combat if Johan is untapped." Bot1 has Johan and an
# Ornithopter from turn 1, Bot2 an Ornithopter of its own. On turn 3 Bot1 says yes: Johan has the ability (CR 113.1a) and
# can't be declared an attacker (CR 508.1c), and the rule takes in Bot1's creatures, not Bot2's nor Bot1's Mox (CR 611.2c), so Bot1's
# Ornithopter attacks and stays untapped (CR 508.1f). Both last only until the combat ends (CR 511.3): in the second main
# phase Johan has no such ability and no creature is under the rule.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Johan
Ornithopter
Plains
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Johan.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
? Bot1.Battlefield.Johan.Keywords = CantAttack
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.LastingRules = Attacking doesn't cause creatures you control to tap this combat if Johan is untapped.
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.LastingRules = (absent)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.LastingRules = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Attackers]
! Bot1.Attack(Johan > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Johan.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Johan.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.LastingRules = (absent)
